---
title: Crispy Brussels sprouts with bacon
servings: 4
yield: 4 as a side, or 2 as a main
tags: [sheet-pan, pork, fall, winter, thanksgiving, christmas]
cuisine: american
time: 35 minutes
source: Best Brussels sprouts with bacon by Food52, https://food52.com/recipes/82177-best-brussels-sprouts-with-bacon-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 450°F.

Spread the @bacon{4%slices}(cut into 1-inch pieces) on a #baking sheet{} and roast ~{5%minutes}.

Meanwhile, toss the @Brussels sprouts{1%lb}(halved), @yellow onion{1/2}(cut into 1/2-inch pieces), @garlic{4%cloves}(smashed, roughly chopped), @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} in a #mixing bowl{}.

Take the sheet out, add the sprouts and toss them in the bacon fat with a spatula. Lay them cut side down in an even layer.

Roast ~{20-30%minutes}, turning the sprouts and the sheet halfway, until the bacon is crisp and the sprouts are tender and charred in places.

Drizzle over the @maple syrup{1%tbsp}, toss, and roast a few minutes more, until as crisp as you like.

Straight out of the oven, sprinkle with the @apple cider vinegar{1%tsp} and @red pepper flakes{1/8%tsp}. Toss, taste, and adjust the salt, heat and vinegar.

> For the crispiest sprouts use a bare metal sheet, no parchment, and leave them alone once they are cut side down. Scatter the loose leaves on after ~{10%minutes}. They are crispest straight from the oven but good warm or at room temperature.
